# Tasks' realm views (sd:5064): which checkouts are which part of your life.
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/realms.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system); the lines below
# are examples. Paths are your own, so the real list stays outside the checkout.
#
# Pipe-separated, one glob per line:
#
#   realm|<id>|<label>|<glob>
#
# <id> is lower case with hyphens, and not personal, hoa, home or all. Each realm
# is a view on Tasks, after Personal and before HOA, Home and All, in the order
# of its first line. A task belongs to the first realm with a glob that matches
# its repo path (* matches across folders; ~ is your home folder). A task with no
# repo, or a repo no line matches, is Personal; a report is in no realm.
# Without this file a task in a repo shows only under All, and the page says why.

realm|work|Work|~/repos/example-work/*
realm|brand|Brand|~/repos/example-brand/*
realm|brand|Brand|~/repos/brand-site
